{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>How can I bear alone.</b> If I were to say, to receive pay, I cannot — this is what I said to you: not on my own do I say this to you, but from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Your burden.</b> This teaches that Israel were טַרְחָנִין — one of them would see his opponent winning the case, and say: I have witnesses to bring, I have proofs to bring, I keep piling more judges upon you." "<b>And your conflict.</b> This teaches that they were heretics: Mosheh went out early — they said, what did the son of Amram see to go out? Perhaps things are not calm in his house. He was late to go out — they said, what did the son of Amram see not to go out? What do you suppose? He is sitting and plotting against you evil schemes and devising against you plots." "<b>And your multitude.</b> This teaches that they were grumblers (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:24.625559697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}